Z||000007||Lisa 86 2m4||07-31-2001||07:34 PM||||Hey Mike,<BR>Considering I was born and raised in Binghamton....good luck at finding anything! However, if memory serves, there is an AutoZone in Endicott on E. Main St., Harco Auto., Carquest, Parts Plus and Napa. Or go to <A HREF="http://www.jcwhitney.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jcwhitney.com</A>  look under air filters, they ship pretty fast.  Hope any of this helps!||||reg||7
Z||000008||theogre||07-31-2001||08:39 PM||||Go to one of the places that carries K&N and look up the one you want in the K&N catalog and order it at the parts counter. You'll likely have to pay up front. Almost no-one has all the K&N catalog instock but they can usually get them quick enough.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GTMike||07-31-2001||11:46 PM||||found one today. its a good kind  it doesn't have the caped end. its a cone with a littler cone going back in on the end.  any one get it.<P>well i make my intake and its freakin great.  ass o meter feels it pulling more from 3500 up to 5000.    and a really cool sound  scarry sound  would make ricers run the other way.   i took some pictures but wont get them developed for a few days i'll post them at the end of the week||||reg||1
